@startuml
title GET /api/ai-agents-teams/{address}/{id}/published-channels — three-valued per-channel reachability
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Interfaces panel" as UI #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.publishedChannels(id)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "Observer + PDS" as Sources #FFF1CC

UI -> SDK : publishedChannels(id)
SDK -> API : GET .../{address}/{id}/published-channels
API -> Domain : aggregate

group Three independent reads (a failure in one never blanks another)
Domain -> Sources : f1r3sky: published_state — chain record\nreconciled against the PDS\n(account_exists stays three-valued)
Domain -> Sources : mail: getChannelBindingsForTeam(id),\nfiltered to channel "mail"
note right of Domain #FFF6C9
Mail reachable is ALWAYS absent:
embers does not probe SMTP, so the
answer is unknown by design — never
falsely asserted, never rendered
as "missing".
end note
Domain -> Sources : chat: list every deployed version's URI\n(each deploy mints a fresh one), then\nlistGrantsForTeam per URI; count active\n(unrevoked) chat grants + distinct principals
note right of Domain #FFF6C9
The gateway dials out and exposes no
status surface, so active grants are
the honest maximum embers can report
for chat.
end note
end

Domain --> API : PublishedChannels { firesky?, mail[], chat }
API --> SDK : 200 PublishedChannels
SDK --> UI : rows rendered by the three-valued\ndiscipline (reachable / unknown / unreachable)
@enduml
